{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:92d36bc1a262e65b","name":"Watch-Beast","source":{"id":"source:reference-92d36bc1a262e65b","title":"Watch-Beast","revision":20992,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:57:09Z","sha256":"8f03f667cef475bb2ab5490843bd008fcfd1121905db1693a0b1e854e5fbe7d4","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20992","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Watch-Beast&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-92d36bc1a262e65b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Watch-Beasts originate on the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gamorr"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gamorr","referenceId":"reference:2267314e8963e4ee"},", but various subspecies are found throughout the galaxy, most notably on the Imperial world of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sirpar"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sirpar?action=edit&redlink=1"},". These enormous beasts resemble both bears and pigs, with squat but powerfully built furry bodies and porcine faces and snouts. A Watch-Beast has two large horns and massive tusks, which are primarily for display but can also be used to gore prey. The Watch-Beast's meaty legs are covered in dense fur and end in short, dull claws.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As its name implies, a Watch-Beast excels at guarding an area and alerting its owner to potential threats. It is extremely territorial and considers any creature, or even a moving object such as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeder"},", to be a threat. When alerted to the presence of an intruder, a Watch-Beast releases a croaking bark that can be heard for nearly a kilometer. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gamorreans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gamorreans"}," steal cubs from their mothers and bond them to a single individual, whom the Watch-Beast obeys utterly. Most owners make a point of training their Watch-Beasts to ignore allies and friendly ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," in order to keep the Watch-Beast from barking- or attacking- every time someone arrives or leaves.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Watch-Beast Statistics (CL 9)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 10\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +2; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", Scent, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +16\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 14), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 17, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 14; Defensive Awareness\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 115, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 27\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 8 Squares; ",{"tag":"a","children":["